{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/117032-ideal-locations-for-promethean","id":117032,"title":"Ideal locations for Promethean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-21T10:44:20-07:00","id":117032,"title":"Ideal locations for Promethean","content":"What are the locations (cities/countries) you consider to be ideal for the purposes of running Promethean?<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm thinking about running Promethean in Delhi or Phnom Penh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:58:40-07:00","id":117040,"title":"","content":"In terms of Delhi, the first wife of Shiva was torn to pieces and later reborn/reincarnated. Kind of relevant to the Ulgan. She has more to do with Varanasi, however, which would be a natural Promethean centre, because of its connection to rebirth and redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:47:12-07:00","id":117068,"title":"","content":"The fertile crescent. It's both a place where most modern political games are played and the ancient birthplace of most modern civilisation (which in Promethian is probably more important than the birthplace of mankind) and full of regimes of varying stability and fundamentalism (suited for the most Abrahamic of the gamelines).<br /> <br /> You could do an epic chronicle that starts shortly before the first Afghanistan war and ends maybe around today in the post Arab-spring world. Players will witness the changes wrought by charismatic ideologues, dictators and foreign superpowers through an alchemical lens; broken up with trips to the wastes where you find track down places from the bible which are relevant to current events, such as the ruins created by the 10 Plagues around the Egyptian Revolution.<br /> <br /> The grand finale will be a debate between the players and God at the gates of Eden itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:46:35-07:00","id":117139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> first Afghanistan war </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the First Anglo-Afghan War?<br /> <br /> In any case, a game set in Afghanistan over a few centuries would be a great idea. The clashing of different modes of dealing with modernity would be really interesting to compare to Prometheans on their pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:54:22-07:00","id":117143,"title":"","content":"Nope, I meant the first ever war in Afghanistan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously, I think it would work if you start with either the First-Afghan War or the Soviet one depending on how ambitious you are. There's more than enough history from, say, 1977 onwards with proxy plays in the middle east to pull of a &quot;reflection of global politics&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if you did go back to the First-Afghan War, I would definitely go for a larger section of the middle east. You'd want to visit the Gallipoli Campaign for example, as foreshadowing for the end of the British Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-21-2014, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T15:02:33-07:00","id":117670,"title":"","content":"Detroit - I can think of fewer American cities that exemplify urban decay and the modern Wasteland","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T14:35:22-07:00","id":119975,"title":"","content":"The &quot;official&quot; chronicle, detailed in the 5 promethean books, mixes it up by having the characters travel to different cities each with a different feel. If you own the &quot;Chicago&quot; book, you could have some interesting cross-over possibilities. The Vampire Requiem book &quot;Nomads&quot; provides some useful information if you wanted to do a traveling Vampire and Promethean game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}